# SRG-APP-000374-WSR-000172  -  CAT II
# The web server must generate log records that can be mapped to Coordinated
# Universal Time (UTC) or Greenwich Mean Time (GMT).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000374-WSR-000172
group:           V-206425
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001890
control_rev5:    AU-8

contribution:    Splunk Web is a component of the same Splunk Enterprise instance rather
                 than a separate web server, so the application names its own access log
                 and, where that log is indexed, maps its timestamps to UTC through the
                 splunk_web_access source type.

governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           props.conf [splunk_web_access] TIME_PREFIX non_empty
check:           props.conf [splunk_web_access] TIME_FORMAT non_empty
check:           props.conf [splunk_web_access] TZ non_empty
check:           props.conf [splunk_web_access] TZ_ALIAS present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The time zone of the splunkd process that writes the access record comes
                 from the host process environment, which is set outside the Splunk
                 configuration files assessed here.
external:        Host clock accuracy and synchronization to an authoritative time source
                 are operating system and time service functions.
external:        Where the Splunk Web access log is monitored into an index by a different
                 instance, that instance's input configuration carries the remainder.

citation:        web.conf.spec:16 [settings], :871 log.access_file = <filename> default
                 web_access.log; props.conf.spec:529 TIME_PREFIX, :554 TIME_FORMAT, :580
                 TZ, :592 TZ_ALIAS.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: Splunk Web names no access log,
                 or the splunk_web_access source type states no TIME_FORMAT and no TZ, so
                 the access record timestamps are not deterministically mapped to UTC or
                 GMT by application configuration.
